comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:49:39.419Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Reviewed complete all-status PM metadata, active comments/notes/learnings, prior API/compatibility/coverage/format plans, official latest releases, live 10.11.11 schema, help, dependencies, and sanitized research output before creation; no duplicate current-version discovery or read-only scope correction item exists."
  "2026-08-06T18:02:37.684Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Implementation checkpoint: schema versions and dynamic compatibility aliases are operational; read-only coverage reports the correct 275-tool safe scope instead of comparing 405 total tools to GET/HEAD operations. No Jellyfin mutation was performed and no credentials were written to the repository."
  "2026-08-06T18:13:31.277Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Quality checkpoint: release suite, 996-test portable suite, 184-command live read-only suite, dependency audits, Trivy, secret/history scans, current-file zero duplication, PM graph/duplicate/health/storage checks all pass. Repository-wide coverage is 43.76/44.86/54.37/43.51 and legacy jscpd remains red; those pre-existing mandates stay canonical and open as jf-mkzh and jf-lpki."
  "2026-08-06T18:18:20.226Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Correction to the earlier 275-tool checkpoint: that intermediate number exposed 25 non-verb mutations still classified safe. After explicit deny rules, the verified read-only population is 250 tools; 215 map directly, 19 are local, 8 are non-endpoint transports, and 8 safe direct commands remain lexical mapping candidates."
  "2026-08-06T18:30:30.674Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Ready for PR: final validate:release passes; compiled live read-only suite passes 185/185; exact selector validation is fail-before-network; current coverage baseline is 43.78/44.87/54.37/43.53. Only jf-einj is claimed and in progress for the review/merge loop."
  "2026-08-06T18:51:48.642Z",codex-jellyfin-release,"Review pass 1 disposition: CodeRabbit correctly identified that the managed pm-changelog source still recorded @latest and that the explicit sessions logout safety test did not prove pre-network interception. Applied the PM-native exact upgrade to npm:pm-changelog@2026.8.6, added a local request-counting E2E fixture asserting zero requests, and expanded high-quality docstrings on the new release/policy helpers in response to the diff coverage warning. These changes preserve read-only live testing and avoid private configuration in the repository."
  "2026-08-06T18:56:38.354Z",codex-jellyfin-release,"Canonical release gate rerun without a global read-only override passes: 1009 Bun tests plus 999 portable Vitest tests (1 skipped), 9 release-policy tests, build, distribution smoke, 300-line gate, current/history secret scans, dry-run package, npx consumer, bunx consumer, and changelog consistency. The separately compiled E2E safety test ran with JELLYFIN_READ_ONLY=1 and proved sessions logout made zero requests. The earlier environment-forced failure was expected because the unit test intentionally invokes a mutating command to validate error formatting."
  "2026-08-06T19:19:49.943Z",codex-jellyfin-release,"Exact-head review pass 2: CodeRabbit independently confirmed both addressed findings; all confirmation artifacts were positively reacted to. CodeRabbit re-review remained rate-limited, Sourcery skipped/quota-limited, Cubic skipped, and both CodeQL jobs stayed QUEUED with zero runtime for the full 20-minute watcher cap. Fresh inventory found no unresolved review threads. origin/main advanced to the immutable v2026.8.6 release during review, causing a managed-extension manifest conflict; resolution preserves main's release version/changelog and this tranche's exact pm-changelog 2026.8.6 plus TOON 4.1.1 state."
  "2026-08-06T20:14:06.484Z",codex-jellyfin-release,"Final CodeRabbit finding accepted: jellyfin_versions object schemas now reject undocumented fields at envelope, data, release, alias, and compatibility-command boundaries. The internal JSON Schema validator previously ignored additionalProperties entirely, so it now enforces both false and schema-constrained additional properties; 25 focused schema/formatter tests plus typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-08-07T05:16:00.186Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Resumed from the documented external gate after verifying all 48 items, 601 history entries, the 48-node/137-edge graph, zero duplicate clusters across all statuses, current PM 2026.8.6, clean worktree, and PR #53 exact branch identity. CodeQL has since completed successfully; this turn will refresh official/live contracts, privacy-safe settings, exact-head tests, review inventory, and remaining protected-branch gates without creating a duplicate item."
  "2026-08-07T05:19:03.277Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Latest-tooling refresh: official npm metadata now reports pm-changelog 2026.8.7 while pm-cli remains 2026.8.6. Upgraded the managed package through pm upgrade, verified activation/doctor health, and aligned the release pipeline exact pin. During this PM-native workflow, package manage rejected universal JSON/lean controls despite being read-only diagnostics; exhaustive open/closed issue searches found no duplicate, so upstream pm-cli issue #925 records the sanitized defect and workaround."
  "2026-08-07T05:34:47.380Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Live rerun discovery: the original WebSocket acceptance required an ambient KeepAlive within 15 seconds and intermittently failed with a valid duration_reached/event_count=0 result. Two direct probes confirmed server event timing is nondeterministic. Updated the live test to request the official periodic sessions subscription, accept either a bounded duration or count stop, and validate a Sessions record when one arrives; deterministic transport decoding/event delivery remains fully asserted by the synthetic WebSocket integration suite. Focused PM-linked live acceptance now passes without weakening production behavior or generating server mutations."
  "2026-08-07T05:53:47.253Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Exact-head review pass accepted two CodeRabbit findings: the managed-extension file annotation now matches pm-changelog 2026.8.7, and JSON Schema object validation uses own-property checks plus applies strict additionalProperties rules to object union types. Focused schema/formatter regression suite passes 26/26 with typecheck, lint, and diff checks green."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:49:39.419Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Privacy boundary: credentials, server URL, user/server/media IDs, raw live schemas, and payloads remain in environment variables or owner-only ~/.jellyfin-cli. Git and PM retain only public release facts, contract counts, commands, synthetic fixtures, and aggregate outcomes."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:49:39.419Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,A 100 percent operation mapping score does not make read-only tool coverage truthful when mutating tools remain in the compared tool population; operation and tool scope must be aligned before graph or agent conclusions.
  "2026-08-07T05:34:47.727Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Live WebSocket acceptance must prove authenticated connection, subscription, bounds, privacy, and event shape without assuming ambient/control traffic arrives in a fixed window; deterministic delivery semantics belong in the transport-adapter integration test."
