plan_decisions[1]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-06T18:02:35.789Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,Discover release channels from the official Jellyfin GitHub release feed and validate each selected version against the official repository OpenAPI artifact before exposing it.,This avoids hard-coded moving versions while keeping server credentials isolated from public artifact requests.,Unit assertions verify no Jellyfin authorization headers reach GitHub; live command verifies both artifacts.
plan_discoveries[3]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T18:02:36.655Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"The stable local server and latest official stable release are 10.11.11; latest official preview is 12.0-rc4. Comparing stable to preview reports 39 breaking, 129 review, and 26 nonbreaking changes."
  "2026-08-06T18:13:30.692Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,pm-cli 2026.8.6 extends the merge fence with a non-merge rule for managed extension contents and a key-level JSON exception for .managed-extensions.json; pm merge install applied and validated the current contract.
  "2026-08-06T18:18:19.590Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Aligned scoping revealed 25 state-changing commands with nonstandard names were mislabeled read-only-safe, including session logout, remote-control dispatch, playlist sharing, SyncPlay reports, and plugin maintenance. An explicit deny-before-allow policy now blocks them and removes them from agent tool scope."
